// The hopper's body -- the first animal to carry `BrainOutput::Impulse`,
// the ballistic jump the engine has had since 2026-08-29 and no species
// authored until `assets/species/hopper.ron` (2026-09-09). This file exists
// because `place_creature` resolves an animal's material by its species'
// own name (`world.materials.id_of("hopper")`): without it the species
// loads, sits on the COLONY chip, and places zero animals -- the wiring
// audit's own pattern, one file short of hatching.
//
// Same physics as the ant (`ant.ron` above it in the list): a creature cell
// the sweep never moves, flammable on the same terms, live flesh worth the
// same to whatever eats it. What differs is the colour, on purpose: the
// owner's standing ask is that a new creature "not look like a recolored
// ant", and the body plan in the species file is the real answer -- but a
// hopper that hops in ant-black is invisible in flight against the box's
// dark air. Warm ochre, which nothing else in the bed wears: soil is a
// dark brown, plants are green, ants are near-black.
(
    name: "hopper",
    display: "Hopper",
    kind: Creature,
    density: 1.0,
    colors: [
        (156, 104, 34),
        (182, 128, 48),
        (126, 82, 26),
    ],
    flammability: 0.6,
    burn_temperature: 500.0,
    burn_duration: 40,
    burns_into: "corpse",
    heat_conductivity: 0.1,
    food_energy: 480.0,
    penetration_resistance: 0.25,
    food_class: 1.0,
)
